"""Definitions of the 22 OA11 research groups (data for build_groups.py).

Ownership rule: every Official Records record, every state-volume section and every other local text belongs to exactly ONE group (the
register is report_assignments.json for the Official Records, scan_leads.SOURCE_GROUP for the other texts).  A group extracts every row
of work or routine from the texts it owns, whichever unit the row is about (the row's unit_id is the unit, not the group).  Works are
assigned to the group that owns the text most likely to name their builder; a work whose builder only another group's texts name is
extracted there and is cross-listed here.  `targets` are things to look for, not claims.
"""

